  "notes": "Xiaomi MiTV-ASTP1 (codename maverick; China-market firmware), Android 9 (SDK 28),\nfirmware 2.40.641.0514.cn (HyperOS-era CN build), Amlogic/droidlogic, 1 GB RAM, 720p panel.\nStock launcher: com.mitv.tvhome (HOME activity .MainActivityUserMode). It is not in\nKNOWN_STOCK_LAUNCHERS, so install with: STOCK_LAUNCHER=com.mitv.tvhome launcher/build-and-install.sh\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-astp1/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-astp1/debloat.txt com.mitv.tvhome\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nNotes from this firmware:\n- No Google apps at all. Content comes from CN streaming apps: com.ktcp.video (Tencent\nVideo), com.cibn.tv (Youku's TV build \"Kumiao\"), com.hunantv.license (Mango TV - yes,\nthe app itself is in the \"license\" package), com.newtv.cboxtv (CCTV NewTV),\ncom.xiaodianshi.tv.yst (bilibili). The list below keeps them all except NewTV.\n- Network ADB (port 5555) closes on every reboot; re-enable it in\nSettings -> Account & Security -> ADB debugging after each power cycle.\n- mitv.service is the core MiTV service: do not touch it.\n- com.xiaomi.mitv.settings is the ONLY settings UI: nothing on this firmware answers\nandroid.settings.SETTINGS or WIFI_SETTINGS (the launcher's pills need a fallback for that).\n- Casting (com.xiaomi.mitv.smartshare / com.xiaomi.miplay / com.xiaomi.wfdsinkhelperservice /\ncom.duokan.airkan.tvbox) and the app store are deliberately kept.\nNewer China firmware (MiTV-MFTR0 \"freeguy\", Android 14): input routes, Xiaomi settings intents and app\ndiscovery notes in docs/devices/xiaomi-mitv-mftr0-freeguy.txt.\nXiaomi telemetry / push / cloud control",
